          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em global orbit category
            is the unification of all
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbit+categories"} orbit categories
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groups"} groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            are allowed to vary.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-presheaves
            over the global orbit category provide the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} base (∞,1)-topos
            over which the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+equivariant+homotopy+theory"} global equivariant homotopy theory
            (see there) is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            (
            %a{:href => "#Rezk14"}> Rezk 14
            ).
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            The following defines the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+equivariant+indexing+category"} global equivariant indexing category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Glo
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Glo
          #GlobalIndexingCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Glo
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Glo
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
              whose
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                  are
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+groups"} compact Lie groups
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categorical+hom-spaces"} (∞,1)-categorical hom-spaces
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Glo
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi G
                        %mo ,
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Glo(G,H)
                  are the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realizations"} geometric realizations
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
                  of smooth functors and smooth
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Top
                          %mn ∞
                          %mi Grpd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi G
                          %mo ,
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi H
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top\infty Grpd(\mathbf{B}G, \mathbf{B}H)
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Rezk14"}> Rezk 14, 2.1
            )
          .num_defn
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Equivalent models for the global indexing category, def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GlobalIndexingCategory"}
              include the category “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi O
                      %mi gl
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O_{gl}
              ” of (
              %a{:href => "#May90"}> May 90
              ). Another variant is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi O
                      %mi gl
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{O}_{gl}
              of (
              %a{:href => "#Schwede13"}> Schwede 13
              ).
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Rezk14"}> Rezk 14, 2.4, 2.5
            )
          %p
            The following is the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+orbit+category"} global orbit category
          #GlobalOrbitCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Orb
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Glo
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Orb \longrightarrow Glo
            %p
              for the non-full
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} sub-(∞,1)-category
              of the global indexing category, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GlobalIndexingCategory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injection"} injective
              group homomorphisms.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Rezk14"}> Rezk 14, 4.5
            )
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#relation_to_the_local_orbit_category Relation to the local orbit category
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} slice (∞,1)-category
            of the global orbit category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Orb
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Orb
            (the version with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/faithful+functors"} faithful functors
            as morphisms) over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            is the local
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbit+category"} orbit category
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Orb
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi Orb
                    %mi G
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Orb_{/\mathbf{B}G}  \simeq Orb_G
                  \\,.
          %h3#relation_to_orbispaces_and_spaces
            Relation to orbispaces and
            = succeed "-spaces" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-presheaves
            over the global orbit category is that of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbispaces"} orbispaces
          %p
            Accordingly, by the discussion
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "over-%28infinity%2C1%29-topos#SheavesOnBigSite"} here
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} slice (∞,1)-topos
            of orbispaces over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            is that of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-spaces"} G-spaces
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi PSh
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Orb
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi PSh
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Orb
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi PSh
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Orb
                    %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi G
                  %mi Space
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  PSh_\infty(Orb)_{/\mathbf{B}G}
                  \\simeq
                  PSh_\infty(Orb_{/\mathbf{B}G})
                  \\simeq
                  PSh_\infty(Orb_G)
                  \\simeq
                  G Space
          %p
            (where the last step is
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elmendorf%27s+theorem"} Elmendorf's theorem
          %h3#relation_to_equivariant_homotopy_theory Relation to equivariant homotopy theory
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-presheaves
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+equivariant+indexing+category"} global equivariant indexing category
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+equivariant+homotopy+theory"} global equivariant homotopy theory
            and under the canonical projection is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} slice (∞,1)-topos
            over the terminal orbispace is cohesive over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbispaces"} orbispaces
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi PSh
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Glo
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi 𝒩
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi PSh
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Orb
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  PSh_\infty(Glo)_{/\mathcal{N}} \to PSh_\infty(Orb)
                  \\,.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold+cohomology"} orbifold cohomology
            %li
              %p
                %span.newWikiWord
                  cohesive relation between global- and G-equivariant homotopy theory
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/cohesive+relation+between+global-+and+G-equivariant+homotopy+theory"} ?
          %div
            %p
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Global+Homotopy+Theory+and+Cohesion"}> Rezk
                \-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+equivariant+homotopy+theory"}> global equivariant homotopy theory
                \:
            %table
              %thead
                %tr
                  %th
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
                  %th
                    its
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-site"} (∞,1)-site
                  %th
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} base (∞,1)-topos
                  %th
                    its
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-site"} (∞,1)-site
              %tbody
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+equivariant+homotopy+theory"} global equivariant homotopy theory
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi PSh
                            %mn ∞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Glo
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh_\infty(Glo)
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+equivariant+indexing+category"} global equivariant indexing category
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
